{"book":"II Samuel","chapter":24,"entries":[{"id":8693,"title":"II Samuel 24:1","segments":["¶And again the anger of the LORD was kindled against Israel, and he moved David against them to say, Go, number Israel and Judah."],"ref":"II Samuel 24:1","verse":1,"words":[{"text":"¶And again","strong":"H3254"},{"text":" the anger","strong":"H639"},{"text":" of the LORD","strong":"H3068"},{"text":" was kindled","strong":"H2734"},{"text":" against Israel","strong":"H3478"},{"text":", and he moved","strong":"H5496"},{"text":" David","strong":"H1732"},{"text":" against them to say","strong":"H559"},{"text":", Go","strong":"H3212"},{"text":", number","strong":"H4487"},{"text":" Israel","strong":"H3478"},{"text":" and Judah","strong":"H3063"},{"text":"."}]},{"id":8694,"title":"II Samuel 24:2","segments":["For the king said to Joab the captain of the host, which [was] with him, Go now through all the tribes of Israel, from Dan even to Beersheba, and number ye the people, that I may know the number of the people. {Go: or, Compass}"],"ref":"II Samuel 24:2","verse":2,"words":[{"text":"For the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" said","strong":"H559"},{"text":" to Joab","strong":"H3097"},{"text":" the captain","strong":"H8269"},{"text":" of the host","strong":"H2428"},{"text":", which [was] with him, Go now through","strong":"H7751"},{"text":" all the tribes","strong":"H7626"},{"text":" of Israel","strong":"H3478"},{"text":", from Dan","strong":"H1835"},{"text":" even to Beersheba","strong":"H884"},{"text":", and number","strong":"H6485"},{"text":" ye the people","strong":"H5971"},{"text":", that I may know","strong":"H3045"},{"text":" the number","strong":"H4557"},{"text":" of the people","strong":"H5971"},{"text":". {Go: or, Compass}"}]},{"id":8695,"title":"II Samuel 24:3","segments":["And Joab said unto the king, Now the LORD thy God add unto the people, how many soever they be, an hundredfold, and that the eyes of my lord the king may see [it]: but why doth my lord the king deligh